 "description": "Wave-4 blind-spot migration: the speech-act KIND decision (question / instruction / statement) moves from Python (domains/comprehend_text.py::_classify_kind, an if/else ladder) into graph rules the agent can see, experiment on and repair. The adapter writes ONLY the classification SIGNALS onto the inbound Message -- data the parse layer already computed, no decision: sak_pending=1.0 (signals present), sak_ends_q (politeness-stripped text ends with '?'), sak_first_role / sak_first_pos (the first parsed frame element's role/pos). THESE rules then DECIDE the kind and mint it as sak_kind, mirroring _classify_kind's ladder exactly (parity-gated byte-for-byte against tests/fixtures/speech_act_parity/speech_act.json): QUESTION iff ends-? OR subject-aux inversion (first element a function copula/auxiliary) OR a clause-leading wh-focus; else INSTRUCTION iff the first element is a bare content verb; else STATEMENT. Precedence is encoded in the guards (the instruction/statement rules carry Not(<question signals>)), so the three rules are order-independent within one run_rules pass; Eq(sak_kind, null) is the mint-once fixpoint guard. Python reads sak_kind back (a mechanical read) as the general path's kind; comp_kind stays the FINAL comprehension record (the still-Python intercepts -- satisfiable / self-identity / rule-name promotion / table fastpath -- may override it, exactly as before; those are ledger items for later waves). The rules deliberately mint sak_kind, NOT comp_kind: minting comp_kind directly in the pre-comprehension pass would expose a PROVISIONAL kind to the downstream comp_kind-keyed rules (comprehend_instruction etc.) mid-turn -- e.g. 'Tell me about the moon.' is ladder-instruction but final-question -- and that would be a behavior change this wave forbids. EXECUTION (WorldAdapter._graph_kind_for): the agent's HELD copies of these rules are exported from its live engine and run in an ISOLATED engine pass over the live Message's signals (not a full comprehend() fixpoint -- a full pass before the comp_* parse facts exist lets mention-keyed rules fire on a half-ingested turn; measured on the elaboration serve-vs-anaphor race). Held-copy execution is what makes the decision self-repairable: an experiment/adopt edit to a held sak rule changes the live classification with no Python change. Single-anchor match on agent -received-> m (the sd 'agent observed obs' pattern).",
